Here’s a **simple, clean Todo List** made using **pure HTML, CSS, and JavaScript** with **basic DOM manipulation** (`document.getElementById`, `createElement`, etc.).

You will have **three separate files**:

---

# ✅ **1. index.html**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Simple Todo List</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <h2>Todo List</h2>

        <div class="input-row">
            <input type="text" id="todoInput" placeholder="Enter a task">
            <button id="addBtn">Add</button>
        </div>

        <ul id="todoList"></ul>
    </div>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

